Mechanism: RMSNorm drops the mean-centering step and bias term of LayerNorm and rescales activations only by their root-mean-square. This gives a slightly simpler normalization with fewer parameters, which could change optimization dynamics within a short fixed step budget. In a small pre-norm model the representational difference may be minor, so any effect would come mainly from optimization ease rather than capacity.
